==========   rescue-ramfs - Tools for creating a minimal recovery initramfs   ==========

HOW TO USE
Step 1 - Building tools
  $ ./scripts/download-ramfs
  $ ./scripts/build musl
  $ ./scripts/build busybox
  $ ./scripts/build efibootmgr
  $ ./scripts/build fdisk
  $ ./scripts/build e2fsprogs
For network support, also build the following:
  $ ./scripts/build wpa_supplicant
  $ ./scripts/build dropbear

Step 2 - Configuration
  Edit the ESP variable in conf/init to contain the location of your EFI System
    Partition.
For network support:
  $ ./scripts/set-passwd (sets the root password for the initramfs)
  $ ./scripts/gen-wificonf
  Edit the variables in conf/netsetup to reflect your own settings.

Step 3 - Building initramfs
For an image without network support:
  # ./scripts/build ramfs
For an image with network support:
  # ./scripts/build ramfs net

Step 4 - Reboot and test
  Edit reboot-ramfs to suit your preferences and reboot:
  # ./scripts/reboot-ramfs

After running './scripts/build busybox' once, you may configure busybox by running:
  $ ./scripts/build busybox configure

Once you are booted into the initramfs, you should be able to ssh into your
machine as you normally do.


REQUIREMENTS
You need to have minisign installed. You also need the Void release keys. On a Void
Linux system, these can be obtained by installing void-release-keys. For obtaining
the keys on a non-Void system, please consult:
 https://docs.voidlinux.org/installation/index.html#verifying-digital-signature


BUILD DURATIONS
These values were recorded on a low-spec potato from 2018. Your own build durations
will most certainly be shorter than these.

	musl				21 min
	busybox				31 s (excluding time to download archive)
	efibootmgr			22 s
	fdisk				1m 29s
	e2fsprogs			24 s
	wpa_supplicant		55 s
	dropbear			41 s
